WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.800
In an old house, an old woman gathers her&nbsp;
knitting supplies. This is a special project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:13.680
for a little boy named Tommy she loves dearly.&nbsp;
She knits furiously, and soon the mix of cotton,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:19.760
synthetic fiber, and cloth of every color turn&nbsp;
from raw materials into something else - a teddy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:25.760
bear. She puts the finishing touches on the&nbsp;
bear - this is a very special bear, after all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.320
and sends the patchwork bear off to its&nbsp;
destination with a red get-well card.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:35.120
The card is labeled “Kairos the Bear”,&nbsp;
and inside she writes a personal note.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:36.000
“To Tommy,

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.800
Because only time can mend all wounds.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.000
Love, Grammy”

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
But this package full of love&nbsp;
would never reach its destination.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.160
SCP-2295 was found at the site of a crashed&nbsp;
mail truck, and it looks exactly like a standard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:56.000
handmade teddy bear - with one difference.&nbsp;
On the left side of its chest, just under its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.640
jaunty tan bow, it wears a heart shaped pin.&nbsp;
But not a standard cartoon heart - this is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:10.080
disturbingly realistic, anatomically correct pin&nbsp;
of a heart organ. And that’s because SCP-2295 has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:15.680
a specific purpose - and it’s one that has&nbsp;
everything to do with actual human organs.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:22.640
SCP-2295 spends most of its time completely inert,&nbsp;
spending its days as just another cuddly stuffed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:28.320
toy. Tests performed on the toy revealed it had&nbsp;
no unusual properties and seems to be a normal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:35.440
handmade keepsake - that is, until someone is&nbsp;
injured in its presence. Not any injury will do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:39.520
a paper cut or even a broken arm for&nbsp;
example won’t do much to activate its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.560
anomalous properties. But if it detects a&nbsp;
critical injury to a human organ nearby,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:48.400
it will trigger its secret power&nbsp;
- one that the Foundation is still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:54.720
trying to figure out how it works.&nbsp;
Because SCP-2295 is a miracle worker.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:59.520
When it senses the presence of someone with a&nbsp;
serious injury to an organ and is within two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:06.560
meters of them, SCP-2295 springs into action.&nbsp;
Suddenly, from unknown sources, the bear will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:11.680
produce objects including scissors, white thread,&nbsp;
and sewing needles or a crocheting hook from its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.880
mouth. If there are any crafting supplies&nbsp;
on hand, it will incorporate those as well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:22.080
And then, it gets to work. Despite only having&nbsp;
hands made of fabric and stuffing with no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.640
fingers, the anomalous bear is still able&nbsp;
to craft what will end up being a patchwork&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:33.040
recreation of the damaged human’s organ. Cute, if&nbsp;
a little creepy, but that’s just the beginning.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:38.480
The injured person mysteriously falls unconscious,&nbsp;
and the patchwork organ, which the Foundation has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:46.320
designated as an SCP-2295-1 instance, will&nbsp;
disappear. The SCP-2295-1 instance will then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:52.320
physically replace the damaged organ inside the&nbsp;
person’s body. It’s unknown how this happens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:57.680
the patchwork organ will simply appear inside of&nbsp;
their body, taking the place of the original lung,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:03.360
or kidney, or whichever organ was failing.&nbsp;
It’s unknown where the original organ goes to,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:09.040
since it seems to just disappear as soon&nbsp;
as the 2295-1 instance takes its place.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:13.920
Surprisingly, having this new cotton stuffed&nbsp;
heart of liver does not seem to cause any harm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:19.360
and in fact, it works exactly like the real thing.&nbsp;
There are never any of the usual issues that come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:24.240
with a transplant like the risk of it being&nbsp;
rejected by the body, as the organic tissue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:29.440
seems to have no issue connecting with the organ&nbsp;
and treating it like it was there all along.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:35.440
In all instances of SCP-2295 performing&nbsp;
this adorable but rudimentary surgery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:38.640
the subjects have made a&nbsp;
full and complete recovery.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.080
SCP-2295 might sound like a miracle worker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.800
but that isn’t to say that its abilities&nbsp;
aren’t without their own set of complications.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:52.720
When faced with two injured subjects, SCP-2295&nbsp;
seems to always gravitate towards fixing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:57.280
younger subject up first - maybe owing to&nbsp;
its creation by a grandmother who wanted to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:03.120
heal whatever was ailing her grandson. No one&nbsp;
knows who Tommy was or exactly what disease or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:08.160
injury he was recovering from, but his grandmother&nbsp;
clearly felt it was serious enough to create this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:14.640
special bear for him. While SCP-2295 will heal&nbsp;
anyone, it seems to be primarily a guardian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:20.720
for the young. And it takes its duties very&nbsp;
seriously - even to the point of self-sacrifice.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:25.760
While SCP-2295 is able to pull some&nbsp;
of its supplies out of thin air,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:32.400
it still always needs some raw materials to craft&nbsp;
the new organ, including fabric and stuffing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:39.040
And if there are none available, SCP-2295 will&nbsp;
obtain them the hard way. The patchwork bear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:44.240
will sacrifice its own body, tearing itself&nbsp;
open and removing any fabric or stuffing it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:50.480
needs without any concern for its own well-being,&nbsp;
in order to craft a new organ for its patient.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:56.160
It slowly regenerates its own stuffing, at&nbsp;
the rate of around a gram of stuffing per day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.440
but it needs to harvest fabric&nbsp;
to repair its outer layer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:05.360
which the Foundation happily makes available to&nbsp;
it, offering it a variety of patterns and types.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:09.920
It’s no surprise that a teddy bear capable&nbsp;
of healing mortal wounds would be of great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:15.360
interest to the SCP Foundation, and as soon&nbsp;
it was recovered from the crashed mail truck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:20.960
they immediately began tests to find out more&nbsp;
about it. Could it heal literally any organ?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:25.840
Were there any limits to its abilities?&nbsp;
There was only one way to find out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:31.760
and the Foundation had the perfect test subjects&nbsp;
- D-Class Personnel, whose interactions with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:38.480
non-cuddly teddy bear SCPs frequently left them&nbsp;
with critical external and internal injuries.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:44.560
The first test subject brought in, D-2353, a&nbsp;
thirty-eight year old man who was in poor health&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:50.560
not due to his work as a D-class personnel, but&nbsp;
from his years and years of heavy smoking. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:55.680
lungs were seriously damaged, which gave him&nbsp;
trouble breathing and made any serious physical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:01.920
exertion extremely difficult. He wasn’t critically&nbsp;
injured or in danger of dying immediately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:10.080
but that didn’t matter to SCP-2295. D-2353 quickly&nbsp;
passed out and the bear sprang into action.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:16.240
It proceeded to take two textile swatches, one&nbsp;
black and one red, and create a pair of fabric&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:22.240
lungs which it installed in the patient.&nbsp;
When he awoke, D-2353 found he had full,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:26.960
healthy lung function again, as if&nbsp;
he’d never picked up his deadly habit.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:29.280
But now the Foundation researchers needed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:34.800
know how SCP-2295 would do with&nbsp;
even more complicated ailments.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:41.520
D-3542 was fifty years old and his heart was not&nbsp;
in good shape. Not only did he have a serious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:47.600
case of atherosclerosis, which is a disease where&nbsp;
cholesterol plaque builds up and blocks blood flow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:52.720
and can put you at a serious risk of a heart&nbsp;
attack, but he also had an irregular heartbeat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:58.240
This D-Class was in bad shape, but&nbsp;
that was no problem for SCP-2295,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:03.760
who took a collection of different colors of yarn&nbsp;
and a crocheting hook and created a plushy heart.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:08.560
Just like the lungs had acted as if they were&nbsp;
completely regular organs, after the heart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:14.000
anomalously ended up inside the man’s chest it&nbsp;
began to beat normally and performed all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:20.160
complicated functions of a human heart. But there&nbsp;
was one detail that shocked the onlooking doctors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:25.280
Before the yarn organ had vanished, the&nbsp;
doctors had seen that it was beating.

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:33.600
So is there any organ that SCP-2295 can’t replace?&nbsp;
That was about to be tested when D-7894 was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:38.720
brought in. A twenty-four-year-old woman, she&nbsp;
had suffered serious burns all over her torso,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:43.840
left abdomen, and right leg. She was brought&nbsp;
in and sedated to numb the agonizing pain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:50.480
and researchers were worried that they had come&nbsp;
up against the limit of SCP-2295’s abilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:58.080
since the skin is the largest organ after all. But&nbsp;
SCP-2295 wasn’t fazed at all, the bear immediately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:03.600
started sewing segments of patchwork fabric and&nbsp;
layering them onto the damaged skin, replacing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:10.320
dermis and epidermis layer by layer. Unlike the&nbsp;
other cases, these replacement organs are visible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:17.440
and D-7894 now has patchwork skin, just&nbsp;
like her talented surgeon. And amazingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:21.760
the fabric has the same sense of&nbsp;
touch that her regular skin did.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:30.320
The final test of SCP-2295’s abilities came with&nbsp;
D-2723, who was only eighteen years old. This last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:35.280
minute D-Class test was performed because he was&nbsp;
showing signs of a severe cerebral hemorrhage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:40.160
the kind that would cause brain damage in only&nbsp;
minutes, and would be followed soon after by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:47.040
complete brain death. SCP-2295 sprung to life,&nbsp;
but as soon as it examined the test subject,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:51.760
it became distressed. It started frantically&nbsp;
grasping at random materials around it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:56.880
as if it didn’t know what to do with them. Then,&nbsp;
it reached inside itself and provided a large&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:03.280
chocolate bar, which it offered to the subject,&nbsp;
sadly to no effect. It then seemed to admit defeat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:08.400
as it grabbed tightly onto the subject’s leg.&nbsp;
Observers reported that it was leaking a tear-like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:14.400
solution from its small knitted eyes as it&nbsp;
embraced the dying D-Class in his final moments.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:22.080
Sadly, it seems that the human brain is the&nbsp;
one mystery that even SCP-2295 can’t solve.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:28.800
SCP-2295 appears to pose no threat to anyone&nbsp;
and was classified as safe after testing. It’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:33.920
inactive when not in the presence of an injured&nbsp;
person and has never displayed hostile instincts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:38.320
when active. The Foundation determined that&nbsp;
it should be stored in a standard containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:43.680
locker in Site-37, where it can be kept safely&nbsp;
until it’s needed for tests or to repair an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:50.160
injured SCP personnel. Access is limited to&nbsp;
those with Level 3 or higher security clearance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:53.360
and any contact with the bear is highly regulated.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:10:00.400
But there is one element of SCP-2295’s existence&nbsp;
that continues to worry Foundation staff.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:05.120
SCP-2295’s full origins and&nbsp;
the grandmother who crafted it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:10.560
are unknown. The note it was found with is the&nbsp;
only clue as to where it may have come from,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:15.520
but there are plenty within the Foundation who&nbsp;
are suspicious of the veracity of the letter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:19.840
And they have good reason not to be&nbsp;
too trusting, because another bear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:27.360
with similar abilities exists - and it is&nbsp;
distinctly less benevolent than SCP-2295.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:33.280
SCP-1048 is also a teddy bear, but it is capable&nbsp;
of moving on its own and communicating through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:39.120
gestures at all times. It was initially allowed&nbsp;
to wander around independently and seemed to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:46.080
its home at Site 24 a happier place. But then&nbsp;
it began to display its own crafting abilities.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:52.880
SCP-1048 is able to craft duplicates of itself,&nbsp;
and while the original was seemingly harmless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:58.800
the ones it made were not. These similarly&nbsp;
shaped bears were made of disturbing materials&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:05.680
and were extremely hostile towards any humans&nbsp;
they encountered. The first, SCP-1048-A,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:10.640
was made entirely out of human ears and&nbsp;
when it shrieked, it caused anyone nearby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:16.160
to generate ear-like growths all over their&nbsp;
bodies, eventually causing them to suffocate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:21.120
The creature disappeared - and an on-site&nbsp;
researcher was found to be missing an ear.

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:26.320
The creations of SCP-1048 only got&nbsp;
stranger and deadlier from there.

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:32.160
SCP-1048-B was found in the Site’s cafeteria,&nbsp;
where it was moving around in a halted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:36.800
jerky fashion. It then started bursting at&nbsp;
the seams and revealed what appeared to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:41.600
a human fetus inside. When the creature&nbsp;
screamed, it sounded like a much louder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:47.520
version of a human infant and its croes caused&nbsp;
massive internal damage to anyone around it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:54.400
SCP-1048-B was killed in the ensuing conflict&nbsp;
with Foundation agents, ending its threat.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:58.240
But SCP-1048 was learning deadlier techniques.

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:05.280
When SCP-1048-C was discovered, it looked to be a&nbsp;
teddy bear made entirely out of rusty scrap metal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:09.520
When it was spotted by Dr. Carver&nbsp;
and targeted by Foundation personnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:14.160
the creature turned violent and proved&nbsp;
to have incredible strength - jumping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:18.000
through the agents who were trying to&nbsp;
neutralize it, tearing through their bodies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:23.360
like tissue paper. Attempts to damage it were&nbsp;
unsuccessful, and both it and the bear made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:29.440
out of ears are still on the loose along with&nbsp;
the original SCP-1048. Capturing it is a major&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:35.200
priority for the Foundation - because no&nbsp;
one wants to see what it will create next.

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:39.520
Is there a connection between these&nbsp;
two very different teddy bears?

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:46.320
No one has been able to answer this question. The&nbsp;
origins of SCP-1048 are unknown, and so is any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:52.000
connection to the mysterious grandmother who may&nbsp;
have made Kairos the Bear. But their abilities are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:57.200
similar, with both able to craft living&nbsp;
objects out of seemingly any material.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:02.320
They just have very different ideas as to what&nbsp;
a good use of their crafting abilities are.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:08.880
It’s fortunate that an anomaly as potentially&nbsp;
powerful as SCP-2295 seems to only want to do one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:14.320
thing. To help those in need, especially&nbsp;
those who are the most vulnerable.

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:18.000
For more on another apparently&nbsp;
harmless object with mysterious powers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:24.000
watch “SCP-066 - Eric’s Toy”, or check&nbsp;
out this SCP Explained video instead.

